all ninja on your butt.

249
00:16:17,140 --> 00:16:18,680
I got an idea, dude.

250
00:16:19,040 --> 00:16:21,360
See how far we can toss these dweebs?

251
00:16:21,500 --> 00:16:22,853
Hold on a second, guys.

252
00:16:23,000 --> 00:16:25,353
We gotta find out what happened to them.

253
00:16:25,800 --> 00:16:29,217
Alright, now try to remember
everything you guys did yesterday.

254
00:16:29,300 --> 00:16:31,757
First, I woke up and went to the bathroom.

255
00:16:31,840 --> 00:16:33,016
He means after that.

256
00:16:33,620 --> 00:16:35,177
Ever hear a stepping aside?

257
00:16:35,260 --> 00:16:36,789
Yeah, what's your problem?

258
00:16:37,060 --> 00:16:41,220
The problem shall be yours when I
strip you two fools of your souls.

259
00:16:42,340 --> 00:16:45,222
Does the Grim Reaper know
you raided as Wardrobe?

260
00:16:46,000 --> 00:16:48,420
Ward Valadecu Vestrum Animus.

261
00:16:49,420 --> 00:16:51,420
I just think you just got it bad.

262
00:16:51,600 --> 00:16:54,020
Rise to your feet and duel.

263
00:16:55,980 --> 00:16:57,580
After that, we all duel.

264
00:16:57,800 --> 00:17:00,153
And he squashed Weevil like a cockroach.

265
00:17:01,320 --> 00:17:02,877
Rex was holding us back.

266
00:17:02,960 --> 00:17:07,784
I would have won, but the guy played some
weird card called the Seal of Something.

267
00:17:07,960 --> 00:17:09,580
The Seal of Ori Kalkos?

268
00:17:09,960 --> 00:17:11,400
Yeah, that's it.

269
00:17:11,660 --> 00:17:14,597
And I thought it was one of
those fake knockoff cards.

270
00:17:14,680 --> 00:17:16,637
He didn't happen to mention anything about

271
00:17:16,720 --> 00:17:19,367
a plan to steal the
three Egyptian god cards,

272
00:17:19,460 --> 00:17:20,290
did he?

273
00:17:20,373 --> 00:17:21,203
Wait, they're gone?

274
00:17:21,286 --> 00:17:22,116
He took them.

275
00:17:22,220 --> 00:17:26,040
Well, he and his gang of
thugs did. No way! Seriously?

276
00:17:26,660 --> 00:17:27,490
Seriously.

277
00:17:27,600 --> 00:17:30,160
Hey, we'll win him back one, two, three.

278
00:17:30,700 --> 00:17:34,717
And you two better tell us if you see
three suspicious-looking biker punks,

279
00:17:34,800 --> 00:17:36,240
all right? Sure we will.

280
00:17:36,440 --> 00:17:38,200
You'll be the first to know.

281
00:17:40,440 --> 00:17:42,760
Or not. All right.

282
00:17:43,060 --> 00:17:45,920
The three Egyptian god
cards are up for grabs.

283
00:17:46,260 --> 00:17:47,980
Soon they'll be all mine.

284
00:17:48,620 --> 00:17:49,450
Huh?

285
00:17:51,240 --> 00:17:53,475
First things got freaky at the museum.

286
00:17:53,760 --> 00:17:55,897
Then monsters started
appearing around the world.

287
00:17:55,980 --> 00:18:00,627
and now a gang of bikers are stealing
people's souls with a Duel Monsters card.

288
00:18:00,880 --> 00:18:04,437
I'm thinking all those things have
something to do with one another.

289
00:18:04,520 --> 00:18:05,350
Yeah, really?

290
00:18:05,440 --> 00:18:09,205
I'm thinking, why does all this
weird stuff always happen to us?

291
00:18:09,500 --> 00:18:11,088
You gotta admit, it's true.

292
00:18:11,520 --> 00:18:12,540
Hey, Yuki!

293
00:18:12,980 --> 00:18:15,160
I've been looking all over for you!

294
00:18:16,440 --> 00:18:17,270
Hey!

295
00:18:17,353 --> 00:18:18,183
Uh, hi, you!

296
00:18:18,840 --> 00:18:19,917
Oh, no!

297
00:18:20,000 --> 00:18:24,700
Don't tell me you forgot about me now
that you're a big-time champion duelist!

298
00:18:25,600 --> 00:18:28,920
Yugi, do you have any idea
who this is? Let's see.

299
00:18:29,200 --> 00:18:30,980
This card should ring a bell.

300
00:18:31,240 --> 00:18:32,700
You did give it to me.

301
00:18:36,700 --> 00:18:37,530
Rebecca!

302
00:18:37,613 --> 00:18:38,860
I want you to have this.

303
00:18:39,920 --> 00:18:41,700
That tie's a friendship.

304
00:18:42,360 --> 00:18:43,660
Consider it a gift.

305
00:18:43,940 --> 00:18:45,980
Aw, thank you. Aw, no!

306
00:18:46,340 --> 00:18:47,380
You're that brat!

307
00:18:49,320 --> 00:18:50,150
Hi.

308
00:18:50,580 --> 00:18:51,698
You look different.

309
00:18:51,840 --> 00:18:53,177
Did you get a haircut or something?

310
00:18:53,260 --> 00:18:55,740
No, she traded her teddy bear for glasses.

311
00:18:56,640 --> 00:18:58,380
I don't need a teddy bear.

312
00:18:58,540 --> 00:19:01,420
Because now I have a
boyfriend to protect me.

313
00:19:02,280 --> 00:19:04,240
Excuse me, a boyfriend?

314
00:19:04,980 --> 00:19:07,980
And yet another weird
event to add to the list.

315
00:19:08,280 --> 00:19:10,480
Yep, and this one tops them all.

316
00:19:10,900 --> 00:19:13,140
Probably best if we stay out of it.

317
00:19:13,280 --> 00:19:17,040
Come on, my grandpa really
wants to see you also, Yugi.

318
00:19:17,400 --> 00:19:19,400
Professor Hawkins wants to see me?

319
00:19:22,040 --> 00:19:23,177
Remarkable, isn't it?

320
00:19:23,260 --> 00:19:25,320
That's my boy. Hey, guys!

321
00:19:27,040 --> 00:19:27,870
Yukimoto!

322
00:19:28,240 --> 00:19:30,640
You're just the person I need to see.

323
00:19:30,920 --> 00:19:35,744
I have a theory that all of these monster
sightings have something to do with you.

324
00:19:43,600 --> 00:19:44,900
Here we are, gang.

325
00:19:45,180 --> 00:19:46,520
Home, sweet home.

326
00:19:46,960 --> 00:19:49,820
Wait till the boss hears
we found the Pharaoh.

327
00:20:23,860 --> 00:20:25,500
I'm sorry, I'm sorry.
